EF AI Workspace (#152): the Environment Fund typeface on every screen and preview, the logo on the PDF and the shared
chat, and «بصير» in every tab title. Owner request 2026-10-23: "apply the EF font to everything: the platform, the
outputs and the chats".

- Artifact previews (utils/efFonts.ts): Sandpack runs every preview in a cross-origin iframe that cannot see the app's
  @font-face rules, so Markdown documents, HTML, React, SVG, code and office previews fell back to Tahoma or the system
  face. The app serves the original font files at /assets/fonts/ with Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *, so each preview
  now gets @font-face rules for "Aktiv Grotesk" and "EF Aktiv Grotesk" by absolute URL, a zero-specificity body default
  and, when the page names no font itself, Tailwind's sans stack. Injected after the editor text is merged
  (ArtifactPreview.tsx), so edits keep it. React previews get it from their own /styles.css (sharedFiles): the hosted
  bundler serves its own page and ignores /public/index.html. Fonts the model sets still win.
- Mermaid (MermaidSvg.tsx): diagrams were <img src=blob:>, and an image cannot use web fonts, so labels were measured
  in Aktiv Grotesk and drawn in a fallback face. They are now drawn inline in a shadow root, which keeps each diagram's
  style and ids to itself. The SVG is sanitized again for inline use (external links, image sources, @import, external
  url() and escaped CSS are dropped), a diagram's own %%{init}%% can no longer change the theme, CSS or fonts, and
  rendering waits for the font. SVG and PNG exports embed the font (Regular, plus Bold when used).
- Code: Arabic in code falls back to the brand face (Tailwind mono stack, print view). Avatars, which are images, use
  Tahoma, the guide's secondary face, instead of Verdana.
- Print/PDF: the blue horizontal logo at the top right (guide p17), symbol at the 1.5 cm print minimum (p9); the print
  dialog waits for the fonts and the logo (at most 3 s) instead of a fixed 400 ms.
- Shared chat: the logo above the title (40 px, the digital minimum). The service worker precaches the logo for the
  offline page.
- Tab titles: the Marketplace, Insights and fallback titles use the platform's name, not "LibreChat".
- Tests: the document-title tests expect the platform's name, and the Mermaid ones the EF light theme of 0023.

